  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda Country Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TradeMark Africa&apos;s Uganda Country Programme works to reduce trade costs, strengthen regional connectivity, and build a more competitive and inclusive trading economy, operating along the Northern Corridor since 2011 in alignment with Uganda&apos;s Vision 2040, NDP IV, and AfCFTA and EAC integration commitments. The Programme has delivered a comprehensive portfolio of physical and digital trade infrastructure, including six One Stop Border Posts at Elegu, Mutukula, Busia, Mirama Hills, Goli, and Ntoroko, the Gulu Logistics Hub providing inland container handling and warehousing capacity, and the Uganda Electronic Single Window now integrating over 30 government agencies and contributing to a 79% reduction in import and export processing times &#x2014; while partnering with the Uganda National Bureau of Standards (UNBS) to decentralise testing laboratories to Mbale, Gulu, and Mbarara. The current strategy deepens this foundation through smart border upgrades including the climate-resilient Elegu Cross-Border Market, scaling of e-certification systems, NTB platform integration with the EAC, and inclusive trade programming.</narrative>
  </description>
